==English==

===Etymology===
{{glossary|ellipsis|Elliptical}}, since the {{glossary|agent noun|agent}} (any intoxicating [[substance#Noun|substance]]) is [[implicit#Adjective|implicit]] because it is [[understood#Adjective|understood]] in [[context#Noun|context]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-under the influence.ogg|a=AU}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} While [[intoxicated]] or [[inebriated]], in any degree from mildly [[impaired]] to [[stupefied]], by a [[mind-altering]] [[substance]], typically [[alcohol]]; thus, especially, [[drunk#Adverb|drunk]].
#: {{ux|en|He was arrested for driving '''under the influence'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|He was fired for showing up '''under the influence'''.}}

====Derived terms====
{{col|en|driving under the influence}}

